        "orario": "04:45",
        "timestamp": 1777257924,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Live Middle East war live: Putin receives Iran’s foreign minister amid stalled US-Iran talks Middle East Issued on: 27/04/2026 - 04:45 Modified: 27/04/2026 - 05:09 Russian President Vladimir Putin plans to meet with Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi on Monday, Russian state media reported. Russia and Tehran, who are both subject to fierce Western sanctions, have developed an increasingly close relationship in recent years. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates. 27/04/2026 - 05:09 China's industrial profit growth quickens even as Iran war heightens risks Profits at ​China's industrial firms grew at their quickest pace in half a year last month, adding to broader signs of an uneven economic recovery in the first quarter as policymakers brace for the impact of the Middle East war. The ​country's export ‌engine stuttered last month while retail sales and industrial output cooled, although producer prices ⁠emerged from a years-long deflationary stretch, a shift that analysts warn could leave companies boxed in by rising costs but limited pricing power as ‌demand remains fragile. 27/04/2026 - 04:53 Hengli Petrochemical shares dive after US imposes Iran oil sanctions Hengli ​Petrochemical shares ​fell 10% on ​Monday ‌after ⁠the ‌US ⁠last week imposed sanctions ​on ‌the firm, ‌one ​of China's largest independent refiners, ​for ​allegedly buying ​Iranian ​oil. 27/04/2026 - 04:37 Iran FM arrives in Saint Petersburg for Putin talks, Iranian state media Iran's Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi arrived in Saint Petersburg on Monday, state media reported. \"He arrived early on Monday morning with the aim of meeting and holding talks with Russian President Vladimir Putin,\" Iranian state news agency IRNA posted on Telegram. Moscow's TASS news agency confirmed earlier that Putin plans to meet Araghchi, citing Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov. Yesterday's key developments: President ​Donald ​Trump has said Iran can reach ​out to ‌the US by telephone ‌if it ​wants to negotiate an end to ​the ​war between ​the two ​countries. Two Israeli political heavyweights have said they would join forces in upcoming elections in a shared effort to unseat longtime Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu . Lebanon 's Hezbollah has accused Israel of violating the ceasefire and has warned that the violations will be met with resistance. (FRANCE 24 with AFP, AP and Reuters)"
